          <div class="ac-title">Anti-Sex-Trafficking Vote (2026)</div>
          <div class="ac-body">Rabb was the sole "no" vote against advancing two anti-sex-trafficking bills out of a PA House committee. He argued the legislation could inadvertently penalize parents for paying friends or relatives to care for their children. Critics called it an inexplicable vote on a widely supported issue. Rabb defended his reasoning in detail. <a href="https://www.phillyvoice.com/pennsylvania-primary-congress-dwight-evans-sharif-street-chris-rabb-ala-standford/" target="_blank">PhillyVoice coverage →</a></div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="alert-card warning">
        <div class="ac-icon">⚠️</div>
        <div>
          <div class="ac-title">Treasurer Fraud Scandal (2025–2026)</div>
          <div class="ac-body">Former treasurer Yolanda Brown allegedly embezzled $160,825 in 40 transactions. The scandal temporarily devastated the campaign's finances. Rabb disclosed proactively and reported to the FEC. Brown has faced similar allegations across four states. This is not a story about foreign money — it is a story about campaign financial controls and due diligence in hiring. <a href="https://www.inquirer.com/newsletters/morning/yolanda-brown-campaign-finance-fraud-chris-rabb-20260302.html" target="_blank">Inquirer investigation →</a></div>
        </div>
